### P68871 – Hemoglobin Subunit Beta (HBB)

P68871 represents the beta subunit of human hemoglobin, a protein responsible for transporting oxygen from the lungs to body tissues and
carrying carbon dioxide back to the lungs. It is one of the most extensively studied proteins because of its essential physiological role
and its association with disorders such as sickle cell disease and β-thalassemia, making it a valuable model for protein analysis.

